{
  "id": "minimum-value-to-get-positive-step-by-step-sum",
  "questionId": "minimum-value-to-get-positive-step-by-step-sum",
  "slug": "minimum-value-to-get-positive-step-by-step-sum",
  "title": "Minimum Value to Get Positive Step by Step Sum",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Prefix sum",
  "patterns": [
    "prefix sum"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "startValue just shifts every running total by the same constant. what single number about the array determines whether any shift keeps everything at least 1?",
    "the lowest point the unshifted running sum ever reaches",
    "compute the prefix sum as you scan and track its minimum value across the whole array",
    "the answer is 1 minus that minimum prefix sum (or 1, if the minimum prefix sum is already at least 0)"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "tracking the minimum element instead of the minimum running prefix sum",
    "forgetting the running sum includes the startValue itself, and off-by-one on the final formula",
    "returning 0 or a negative number when the array is already all non-negative"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array of integers `nums` and a starting value. The step by step sum is computed by adding a `startValue`, then each element of the array in order, tracking the running total at every step.\n\n**Return the minimum positive integer value for `startValue` such that the running total is never less than 1 at any step.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 100",
      "-100 <= nums[i] <= 100"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "every prefix sum is already positive on its own (answer is 1)",
      "a single very negative element"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
